# Notes module

> Read this file first when you resume work on this module, and keep it current (root `CLAUDE.md`,
> "Developing a module"). The project rules are in the root `CLAUDE.md`; the steps in
> `docs/creating-a-module.md`; run `/check-module Notes` before calling the module done.

**Purpose:** TODO: what the module manages, for whom, and what it adds to the back office, the
public site and the API.

## Resources and permissions

Permissions are `notes-<resource>.<operation>`, generated from `Config/Module.php` (never
written by hand).

- `notes-main` (page: `view`): the module's screen `<back office>/notes` (`backend_path('notes')`).
- Default grants: admin `notes-main.*` and the tables' grants below.
- Settings: `Notes.perPage`. Widget `notes.main` (`Widgets/NotesWidget.php`). Scheduled
  task `Tasks/NotesTask.php`.
- Tables: `notes_items` (one migration per table, `down()` implemented).
- `notes-items` (crud: list, show, add, edit, delete, export, import): table `notes_items`, `<back office>/notes/items`. Generated by the code generator (definition in the Devtools wizard / `make:module --definition`).

## Main pieces

- `Config/Module.php` (manifest), `Config/Routes.php` (every back-office route has its `can:`
  filter).
- `Controllers/Home.php` + `Views/index.php` (example screen with the ES-module component
  `Assets/js/notes.js`, `data-component="notes/notes"`).
- `Database/Seeds/NotesSeeder.php` (initial data), `NotesDemoSeeder.php` (demo data:
  `php spark modules:demo Notes`).
- Texts: `Language/{ca,es,en}/Notes.php` (same keys).

